1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,467
You were taught Rome fell in 476.

2
00:00:02,647 --> 00:00:03,463
That's wrong.

3
00:00:03,963 --> 00:00:06,507
At its peak, Rome ruled from Britain to Egypt:

4
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:09,663
three continents, and maybe one in four people on Earth.

5
00:00:10,003 --> 00:00:14,290
In 117 AD, under Emperor Trajan, it hit its biggest size ever.

6
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:15,534
Then it cracked.

7
00:00:15,994 --> 00:00:17,000
Civil wars.

8
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:17,773
Plague.

9
00:00:17,913 --> 00:00:19,577
Invaders on every border.

10
00:00:19,797 --> 00:00:21,083
So Rome split in two.

11
00:00:21,483 --> 00:00:23,639
In 476, the West collapsed.

12
00:00:23,799 --> 00:00:25,159
But the East kept going.

13
00:00:25,519 --> 00:00:28,828
For almost a thousand more years, until 1453.

14
00:00:29,168 --> 00:00:30,768
So when did Rome really fall?

